From c22804a307cb90d491fd221d3150b1f5ba7e3502 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:31:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] The Zune theme: the original Zune's look, for games and
 music

A third UI Theme, and the default: TortOS drawn as the original Zune -
the Zune 30, 80 and 120, the players with buttons - drew itself.

- The top menu is three words over a background picture: zune (the
  music), game boy (the systems and their games), and settings, TortOS's
  own menu, last as on the Zune.
- The twist: a menu's sub-menus run across the top, the list beneath;
  left and right move along the row. Inside an album the other albums
  are the row, as tiny covers. Games twist across the systems.
- Every list starts with shuffle all, or play all under an artist, a
  genre or inside an album. Scrolling fast shows the letter.
- Now Playing: the art over two thirds of the screen, the song beneath;
  the center button for rate, song list, shuffle and repeat; START play
  and pause; the pad to skip, held to scan, and for the volume; Y likes
  the song. A book keeps Muse's own screen and keys.
- The pocket lock: START held on Now Playing, or its "lock screen". The
  screen goes dark and every button is ignored - volume and power too -
  but MENU, which wakes it; a wake with nothing pressed after it locks
  again ten seconds later. The music plays on; Auto Off still ends it.
- The battery beside the clock, top right, on every Zune screen: an
  outline that empties as it runs down, red at 10% and below, a bolt
  beside it on the charger. It replaces the low-battery dot there.
  TORTOS_FAKE_BATT takes a "c" for charging, "40c", to see it.
- Screen Off, first in the settings menu: the pocket lock with or without
  music - dark, every button asleep but MENU, the music playing on, the
  same relock after a wake. Auto Off still powers off once nothing plays.
- The Pixel 2's backlight off is now both switches, bl_power and a level
  of 0; bl_power alone was reported to leave the screen lit. On restores
  the player's level.
- The zune menu offers only what has something in it: no playlists
  without any, no genres without the library index.
- In a game, the in-game menu's Sound row switches what is heard: the
  game, or the music (ADR-0032 quiets the game while the music plays).
  Music with nothing loaded starts the whole library shuffled.
- Liked songs: a like puts the song on Playlists/liked songs.m3u8, an
  ordinary playlist kept in the order liked and shown first among the
  playlists - from memory, so at once. The playlist is the record of
  likes; ratings.tsv keeps the dislikes.
- Music/.zune/library.tsv, from scripts/zunesync.py, gives real titles,
  genres, years and lengths; plays go to plays.log for it.
- The fonts and the background are opened when the theme first draws,
  so the other themes pay nothing for it.

src/zune.c is the drawing, src/zune_music.h the music, main.c the
shelves and Now Playing; ui.c switches the menus' face; controls.c has
the theme's Controls pages.
